# Design system

- Centralize colors, spacing, typography, sizes, radii, shadows, breakpoints, transitions, and z-index.
- Separate primitive palette values from semantic tokens.
- Components consume semantic CSS variables such as `--color-primary`, `--color-surface`, and `--color-text`.
- Do not hardcode brand hex colors, spacing scales, radii, or shadows inside components.
- Theme changes must be possible by editing theme token declarations rather than component files.
- Use one token system for public and admin zones.
- Keep shared primitives in `components/ui/`.
- Use BEM-style class names for non-trivial component styles.
- Prefer scoped component styles; global styles are limited to reset, typography defaults, tokens, and utilities.
- Add a new token only when it represents a reusable design decision.
- Include interactive states: hover, active, focus-visible, disabled, invalid, and loading.
- Preserve accessible contrast and visible keyboard focus.
- Do not use inline styles for static values.
